※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4479

※ A pure function may write its own storage -- an array it made, which is gone
※ when the call ends -- and nothing else.  An array it was handed belongs to the
※ caller, so writing into one is a change the caller can see when the call comes
※ back.

fn clear(v: u8⟦⟧):
    v⟦0⟧ ← 0u8

@[startup, impure]
fn main() → u8:
    let room: mut u8⟦2⟧ = ⟦7u8, 8u8⟧
    clear(room)
    room⟦0⟧
